#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161689 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21f1ec99-e166-5986-a07d-f07be0dfeb31" :knowledge-point/title "Using Row Operations to Create a Column of Zeros in a 4x4 Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "70991204-370a-5804-a04e-7e664db052de" :question/math-academy-id "e-8048" :question/problem "$\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $B$ above. By applying three matrix elementary row operations\n\n1. $R_1:= \\ldots$\n2. $R_3:=R_3-3R_2$\n3. $R_4:= \\ldots$\n\neach of the form $R_i:=R_i+kR_2$, the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B$. What are the missing elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B$, we need to make entries above and below\n\n$$\na_{22}={\\color{blue}\\bbox[lightgray,2pt]{1}}\n$$\n\nequal to ${\\color{red}0}$.\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}R_{1}:=R_{1} - 2R_{2} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{vmatrix}R_{3}:=R_{3} - 3R_{2} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{4}:=R_{4} + 2R_{2} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= B\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing elementary row operations are\n\n$\\qquad$\n\n$$\nR_1:= R_1 - 2R_2\\quad\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\quad R_4:=R_4+2R_2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161690 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "958cdcf3-aaba-5275-85f8-9531f10b3d0e" :knowledge-point/title "Using Column Operations to Create a Row of Zeros in a 4x4 Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "cbf8e85c-ffa6-55b9-a087-2a5272f10f25" :question/math-academy-id "e-8049" :question/problem "$\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -3 & -1 & -6 \\\\ 7 & -2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ -8 & -3 & -6 & -4\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $B$ above. By applying three matrix elementary column operations\n\n1. $C_1:=\\ldots$\n2. $C_3:= C_3 - 4C_2$\n3. $C_4:= \\ldots$\n\neach of the form $C_i:=C_i+kC_2$, the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B$. What are the missing elementary column operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B$, we need to make entries to the left and to the right of\n\n$$\na_{32}={\\color{blue}\\bbox[lightgray,2pt]{1}}\n$$\n\nequal to ${\\color{red}0}$.\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\begin{bmatrix}7 & -3 & -1 & -6 \\\\ 7 & -2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ -8 & -3 & -6 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}C_{1}:=C_{1} + 5C_{2} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & -3 & -1 & -6 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ -23 & -3 & -6 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{vmatrix}C_{3}:=C_{3} - 4C_{2} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & -3 & 11 & -6 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -23 & -3 & 6 & -4\\end{bmatrix} \\mid C_{4}:=C_{4} - 2C_{2} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & -3 & 11 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -23 & -3 & 6 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= B\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding elementary column operations are\n\n$\\qquad$\n\n$$\nC_1:=C_1+5C_2\\quad\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\quad C_4:=C_4-2C_2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161691 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "908b96db-9463-50b5-89a3-056072c930ba" :knowledge-point/title "Using Row Operations to Create a Column of Zeros in a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "399b7598-c793-5032-9f33-ac02c7b85fe1" :question/math-academy-id "e-8050" :question/problem "$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -8 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form $R_i:=R_i+kR_1$, the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B$. What are the elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B$, we need to make the entries below\n\n$$\na_{11}={\\color{blue}\\bbox[lightgray,2pt]{1}}\n$$\n\nequal to ${\\color{red}0}$.\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -8 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}R_{2}:=R_{2} - 2R_{1} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 6 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{vmatrix}R_{3}:=R_{3} + 3R_{1} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 10 & -20\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= B\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$\\qquad$\n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2-2R_1\\quad\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\quad R_3:=R_3+3R_1\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161692 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "85e1fe3f-e85e-5ab4-a594-c55b84bb789a" :knowledge-point/title "Using Column Operations to Create a Row of Zeros in a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "f9912357-1d1d-5413-917e-257dc5dfc0fe" :question/math-academy-id "e-8051" :question/problem "$\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 8 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 9 & 7 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nBy applying elementary column operations of the form $C_i:=C_i+kC_3$, the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B$. What are the elementary column operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B$, we need to make entries to the left of\n\n$$\na_{13}={\\color{blue}\\bbox[lightgray,2pt]{1}}\n$$\n\nequal to ${\\color{red}0}$.\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 8 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 9 & 7 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}C_{1}:=C_{1} + 6C_{3} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -5 & 1 \\\\ -16 & 3 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 7 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{vmatrix}C_{2}:=C_{2} + 5C_{3} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -16 & -17 & -4 \\\\ -3 & -3 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= B\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$\\qquad$\n\n$$\nC_1:=C_1+6C_3\\quad\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\quad C_2:=C_2+5C_3\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162479 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "908b96db-9463-50b5-89a3-056072c930ba" :knowledge-point/title "Using Row Operations to Create a Column of Zeros in a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad6a43ec-d06a-5805-903a-7b82af563185" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{1}:=R_{1} - 2R_{3}$ and $R_{2}:=R_{2} + R_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160507} {:answer/id #uuid "ee487a48-c57f-5440-953d-2e1a0b29979d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{1}:=R_{1} + 2R_{3}$ and $R_{2}:=R_{2} + 2R_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160508} {:answer/id #uuid "2b8f8008-6fb4-5faf-a528-5fd98c80e6c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{1}:=R_{1} - 2R_{3}$ and $R_{2}:=R_{2} - 2R_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160509} {:answer/id #uuid "36cd6545-a02c-55eb-8d8c-b77b5379dd2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{1}:=R_{1} - 2R_{3}$ and $R_{2}:=R_{2} + 2R_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160510} {:answer/id #uuid "4a1e8b86-2d80-5fc3-a4f6-f8b8410e2f80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{1}:=R_{1} + 2R_{3}$ and $R_{2}:=R_{2} - 2R_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160511}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b8f8008-6fb4-5faf-a528-5fd98c80e6c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{1}:=R_{1} - 2R_{3}$ and $R_{2}:=R_{2} - 2R_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160509} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1a5abcf-f87d-517d-962d-40ed18c1b761" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160506}] :question/id #uuid "122850ae-d465-5748-ba36-b0dbdbbedca0" :question